INT. ALBRECHT HOUSE - KITCHEN - MORNING

Yellow curtains, a toaster with a sticker of a cat on it, a calendar with a drawing of the sun. Cereal bowls in a sink.

MINA, 8, in rain boots and pajamas, stands on a chair at the counter. She holds a spoon like a microphone.

A cordless phone on the table rings. She picks it up.

MINA
Hello? This is Mina.

RAYMOND (V.O.)
(phone)
Mina-bean. It's Dad.

MINA
Where are you?

RAYMOND (V.O.)
Airport. The plane is late.

MINA
Again?

RAYMOND (V.O.)
Again. Is Grandma there?

MINA
She's in the garden. She's yelling at the tomatoes.

RAYMOND (V.O.)
(laughing)
Tell her I said hi.

MINA
I will.

She sets the spoon down. Looks at the calendar.

MINA (CONT'D)
Dad? Can you still make my recital?

RAYMOND (V.O.)
Wouldn't miss it.

She nods and hangs up. Outside, a voice calls over the tomatoes. Mina grins.
